What was taken, verbatim, for every challenge in upstream questions/:
  - <id>/template.ts      the challenge's starting template
  - <id>/test-cases.ts    the challenge's own type-level test cases
  - the English README.md description (between the generated header and
    footer markers), embedded in the `prompt` field of
    ../tasks_type_challenges.jsonl
  - title / tags / difficulty from info.yml, in each row's `upstream` field
  - utils/index.d.ts, utils/package.json: the @type-challenges/utils package
    (Equal, Expect, NotAny, ...) from upstream utils/, vendored so grading
    needs no network

What was NOT taken:
  - No solutions. Upstream ships none; every <id>/reference.ts was written
    for this repo and is proven by ../test_grade_tc.py.
  - Nothing from TypeHero (typehero.dev), which is AGPL-3.0.
  - Translations (README.*.md other than English), playground links, the
    "Check out Solutions" / "Share your Solutions" footer links.

Task ids keep the upstream number and slug: questions/00004-easy-pick ->
tc-00004-pick, so every result traces back to its upstream challenge.

CONTAMINATED: the corpus has been public since 2020 and community solutions
to every challenge are widely published. Every row carries
`contaminated: true`; scores on this subset measure recall as much as skill
and must be reported separately from the uncontaminated tasks.jsonl set.

Challenges not shipped are listed, with the reason, in excluded.json.
